Given a rope of length n meters, cut it into multiple smaller ropes such that the product of their lengths is maximized. 
At least one cut is mandatory.

Input: n = 2
Output: 1
Explanation: 1 * 1 = 1

Input: n = 5
Output: 6
Explanation: 2 * 3 = 6

class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int n) {
        if (n == 2) return 1;
        if (n == 3) return 2;

        int product = 1;

        while (n > 4) {
            product *= 3;
            n -= 3;
        }

        return product * n;
    }
}

Time Complexity
O(n)

Space Complexity
O(1)
